WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.958 --> 00:00:07.958
[gentle logo music]

2
00:00:16.333 --> 00:00:17.333
[upbeat piano music]

3
00:00:36.708 --> 00:00:37.542
[dramatic music]

4
00:00:37.625 --> 00:00:38.458
[nickering]

5
00:00:48.875 --> 00:00:49.708
[neighing]

6
00:00:56.917 --> 00:00:58.250
[dramatic orchestral music]

7
00:01:21.375 --> 00:01:22.208
[tense score]

8
00:01:39.208 --> 00:01:40.333
[dramatic drum hit]

9
00:01:42.333 --> 00:01:43.500
[Arabic-inspired score]

10
00:01:50.333 --> 00:01:51.417
[tense dramatic score]

11
00:01:55.625 --> 00:01:58.833
-[news reporter]<i><font color="white"> After surviving</font></i>
<i><font color="white">relentless attacks from</font></i>
<i><font color="white">mercenary forces</font></i>

12
00:01:58.917 --> 00:02:00.500
<i><font color="white">in the escalating oil wars,</font></i>

13
00:02:01.167 --> 00:02:03.750
<i><font color="white">sources tell us that pleas</font></i>
<i><font color="white">have finally been answered</font></i>

14
00:02:03.833 --> 00:02:07.333
<i><font color="white">for the besieged employees</font></i>
<i><font color="white">of Yutime Chinese oil refinery</font></i>

15
00:02:07.417 --> 00:02:08.542
<i><font color="white">in the Middle East.</font></i>

16
00:02:08.625 --> 00:02:11.708
{\an8}<i><font color="white">Professor Cheng,</font></i>
<i><font color="white">Yutime's Director of Operations,</font></i>

17
00:02:11.792 --> 00:02:15.208
{\an8}<i><font color="white">tells us that a private security</font></i>
<i><font color="white">team from China has volunteered</font></i>

18
00:02:15.292 --> 00:02:19.042
{\an8}<i><font color="white">to carry out the high-risk</font></i>
<i><font color="white">mission of extracting her</font></i>
<i><font color="white">trapped oil workers,</font></i>

19
00:02:19.125 --> 00:02:20.667
{\an8}<i><font color="white">who are facing certain death,</font></i>

20
00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:23.500
{\an8}<i><font color="white">and escorting them</font></i>
<i><font color="white">to the safety of the Green Zone.</font></i>

21
00:02:23.583 --> 00:02:24.958
{\an8}[helicopter blades thumping]

22
00:02:30.958 --> 00:02:31.792
[sighs]

23
00:02:38.083 --> 00:02:38.875
-Commander Luo,

24
00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:40.417
we're approaching the LZ.

25
00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:42.750
-Copy, Captain.

26
00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:45.792
[tense score continues]

27
00:02:46.292 --> 00:02:47.458
[automatic rifle clicks]

28
00:03:08.792 --> 00:03:10.625
-[Cheng in Chinese] Dragon Luo.
-[Luo in Chinese] Yes.

29
00:03:10.708 --> 00:03:12.000
-[in Chinese] Professor Cheng,
head of Yutime Oil.

30
00:03:12.083 --> 00:03:12.958
-[in Chinese] Hello, professor.

31
00:03:13.042 --> 00:03:15.375
-[in Chinese]
Thank you for coming 
to rescue us.

32
00:03:15.458 --> 00:03:17.042
-[in Chinese]
Can you bring me up to speed?

33
00:03:17.125 --> 00:03:19.583
-[in Chinese] Of course, follow me. 
-[in Chinese] HaiMing, unload.

34
00:03:19.667 --> 00:03:20.625
You two, follow me. Hurry up.

35
00:03:20.708 --> 00:03:21.542
-[in Chinese] Yes, sir.

36
00:03:21.625 --> 00:03:24.375
-[Cheng in Chinese] We are only
safe inside the refinery.

37
00:03:24.458 --> 00:03:27.083
-[Luo in Chinese] Don't worry,
we're here to escort you out.

38
00:03:27.167 --> 00:03:30.000
Our planes are waiting for you
in the Green Zone.

39
00:03:30.833 --> 00:03:32.000
Do you know who the rebels are?

40
00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.167
-[Cheng in Chinese]
I don't know.

41
00:03:33.167 --> 00:03:35.208
They want us to give
up the refinery.

42
00:03:35.708 --> 00:03:37.167
We've been surrounded
for two weeks.

43
00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:39.542
They launch an attack
every couple of days.

44
00:03:39.625 --> 00:03:41.833
We've increased our security

45
00:03:41.917 --> 00:03:43.875
but if they launch another
attack like yesterday,

46
00:03:43.958 --> 00:03:45.542
we won't make it.

47
00:03:45.625 --> 00:03:46.958
We must evacuate immediately.

48
00:03:47.583 --> 00:03:49.708
-[in Chinese] How many
are we evacuating?

49
00:03:49.792 --> 00:03:52.000
-[in Chinese] Four hundred
and ninety eight including the
children.

50
00:03:53.792 --> 00:03:56.417
-[Luo in Chinese] There's a lot
of things to do before we go.

51
00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:57.750
We plan to leave at dawn.

52
00:04:02.042 --> 00:04:03.458
-Gets it all and
is happy with it.

53
00:04:03.542 --> 00:04:05.917
Looks happy, looks concerned.
He's concerned now.

54
00:04:07.708 --> 00:04:08.542
It's in the sand.

55
00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.458
[boy in Arabic] I made it.

56
00:04:15.958 --> 00:04:16.958
-How's it going, Chris?

57
00:04:17.042 --> 00:04:18.375
-You're late, Henry.

58
00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:19.833
-Jesus, Chris.

59
00:04:22.125 --> 00:04:23.792
Here's your money, as promised.

60
00:04:26.167 --> 00:04:27.875
We go in and out. Nobody hurt.

61
00:04:30.375 --> 00:04:31.625
You're gonna count it?

62
00:04:31.708 --> 00:04:33.375
-Hell yeah, I'm gonna count it.

63
00:04:33.458 --> 00:04:35.208
Listen, you're family
but you're a thief.

64
00:04:35.292 --> 00:04:36.042
-Ah.

65
00:04:36.125 --> 00:04:37.958
-Bald Eagle over there,
he doesn't care if I count it.

66
00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:42.583
Bit of a misread on me,
I think he does care if I count
it.

67
00:04:42.667 --> 00:04:43.875
Or-or was it the nickname?

68
00:04:43.958 --> 00:04:44.958
You guys do nicknames?

69
00:04:46.417 --> 00:04:47.667
You guys don't do nicknames.

70
00:04:48.667 --> 00:04:51.500
Are you kidding me? Nicknames
are like the heart of team
camaraderie.

71
00:04:51.583 --> 00:04:54.292
Huh, you guys are in luck,
nicknames are like my
superpower.

72
00:04:54.375 --> 00:04:55.708
I've been giving 'em out
since peewee football.

73
00:04:55.792 --> 00:04:56.625
-Yeah, bro,

74
00:04:56.708 --> 00:04:58.042
these guys are a
little bit on edge.

75
00:04:58.125 --> 00:04:59.292
-I'm gonna take the edge off.

76
00:04:59.375 --> 00:05:00.042
Okay,
[clears throat]

77
00:05:00.125 --> 00:05:01.125
Bald Eagle,

78
00:05:01.208 --> 00:05:02.375
like the one from the Muppets.

79
00:05:02.917 --> 00:05:03.583
Toothpick.

80
00:05:03.667 --> 00:05:06.125
There's a double meaning.
You'll figure it out.

81
00:05:06.208 --> 00:05:06.958
Uh,

82
00:05:07.042 --> 00:05:08.833
Tomb Raider, because I just--

83
00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:11.500
I just feel like you'll haunt me
long after I'm dead.

84
00:05:11.583 --> 00:05:12.708
[tense score]

85
00:05:16.208 --> 00:05:17.708
[sighs]
Uh…

86
00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:21.917
Full disclosure,
there's a lot going on here, uh…

87
00:05:23.708 --> 00:05:24.792
I'm drawn to "Graffiti"

88
00:05:24.875 --> 00:05:27.167
'cause it looks like some
teenagers vandalized your face.

89
00:05:27.958 --> 00:05:29.000
That's not it.

90
00:05:29.083 --> 00:05:30.875
It's just a start for
me, but I got you.

91
00:05:30.958 --> 00:05:31.750
-Bro,

92
00:05:32.333 --> 00:05:33.750
can you be serious
for one second?

93
00:05:34.625 --> 00:05:36.667
Have you given any more thought
to my plan?

94
00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:39.167
Like, one more mission,
five times the money?

95
00:05:39.875 --> 00:05:41.292
-Can't do it.
I've already done way too much.

96
00:05:41.375 --> 00:05:44.167
-You're telling me this place
couldn't use more money to fix
things up?

97
00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:45.083
-Don't start.

98
00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:47.208
-Yeah, well, it's a big job.

99
00:05:47.292 --> 00:05:48.458
-No.
-Moving target.

100
00:05:48.542 --> 00:05:49.167
-No.

101
00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:50.875
-And it's for Unicorp, bro.

102
00:05:50.958 --> 00:05:51.875
-Not interested.

103
00:05:51.958 --> 00:05:54.833
-You remember that rebel attack
on Area Seven, don't you?

104
00:05:55.708 --> 00:05:57.708
When five of our
guys got popped.

105
00:05:59.833 --> 00:06:01.708
This is the son of a
bitch who armed them.

106
00:06:02.708 --> 00:06:03.833
And right now

107
00:06:03.917 --> 00:06:06.583
a team of mercenaries
is escorting this dirtbag back
to China.

108
00:06:06.667 --> 00:06:07.917
-You wanna take on the Chinese?

109
00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.917
-No, no, no. It's
not the Chinese.

110
00:06:10.625 --> 00:06:12.833
It's an international
criminal, all right?

111
00:06:12.917 --> 00:06:14.958
She's being extracted
on the Highway of Death

112
00:06:15.042 --> 00:06:16.500
back to the Green Zone.

113
00:06:16.583 --> 00:06:17.708
-[boy in Arabic]
Big Dog, come on.

114
00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:19.833
-Stay there, I'll pick you up.

115
00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:22.375
Highway of Death?

116
00:06:23.542 --> 00:06:24.792
The most dangerous
road in the country.

117
00:06:24.875 --> 00:06:25.875
You know that.

118
00:06:26.458 --> 00:06:27.958
You're an idiot
for even thinking about it.

119
00:06:30.292 --> 00:06:31.708
-Yeah, Dad would've
done it, though.

120
00:06:31.792 --> 00:06:32.792
[Chris sighs]

121
00:06:32.875 --> 00:06:33.875
[tense score]

122
00:06:38.167 --> 00:06:39.167
-That was low.

123
00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:43.250
Even for you.

124
00:06:47.542 --> 00:06:48.583
[truck engine starts]

125
00:06:50.542 --> 00:06:51.750
[boy yells excitedly in Arabic]

126
00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:55.625
Keep your eye on the ball, okay?

127
00:06:58.250 --> 00:06:59.292
Almost, almost.

128
00:06:59.375 --> 00:07:01.250
Now let's let it
rip. Hit the mitt.

129
00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:03.042
Whoa.

130
00:07:03.583 --> 00:07:05.083
-Fantastic.
-[car horn honking]

131
00:07:11.208 --> 00:07:12.792
You got it, Funhouse, come on.

132
00:07:14.833 --> 00:07:15.833
-Hey, Soraya.

133
00:07:17.125 --> 00:07:18.125
-Hello, Owen.

134
00:07:19.833 --> 00:07:21.333
-You look beautiful today.

135
00:07:22.375 --> 00:07:23.500
-What? No!

136
00:07:23.583 --> 00:07:26.625
-I hope you don't mind me
saying, but that, um, abaya,

137
00:07:26.708 --> 00:07:29.000
it really makes
your, your skin glow.

138
00:07:29.083 --> 00:07:30.333
-Owen, stop.

139
00:07:32.292 --> 00:07:33.333
-Always working.

140
00:07:33.417 --> 00:07:34.833
-No harder than you, my friend.

141
00:07:34.917 --> 00:07:35.917
[briefcase clatters]

142
00:07:37.208 --> 00:07:38.542
-So what about the pipe?

143
00:07:40.458 --> 00:07:41.458
It's bone dry.

144
00:07:42.042 --> 00:07:43.417
-And you're wasting your time.

145
00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:44.583
Pump's rusted.

146
00:07:46.125 --> 00:07:47.000
Pipe's disconnected.

147
00:07:47.083 --> 00:07:48.375
-[grunts]
-[valve squeaks]

148
00:07:48.458 --> 00:07:49.417
[goat bleating]

149
00:07:51.917 --> 00:07:52.708
[sighs]

150
00:07:54.167 --> 00:07:55.958
-Damn, I hate this company.

151
00:07:56.833 --> 00:07:58.250
-Well, I hate we
don't have water.

152
00:07:58.333 --> 00:07:59.333
-Yeah.

153
00:07:59.583 --> 00:08:00.542
-I mean, I have a little.

154
00:08:00.625 --> 00:08:03.000
I got buckets and charcoal,
so we bring a little at a time,
but

155
00:08:04.208 --> 00:08:05.625
it's not enough.
I mean, they built that dam.

156
00:08:05.708 --> 00:08:07.000
-They cut this place off.
-[Owen sighs]

157
00:08:09.167 --> 00:08:11.542
-If you want,
I can go talk to Unicorp
headquarters

158
00:08:11.625 --> 00:08:13.458
but you know how that goes.

159
00:08:13.542 --> 00:08:14.875
-You want us to
bribe 'em for water?

160
00:08:14.958 --> 00:08:17.417
-There's only one thing
more expensive than oil.

161
00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:19.542
Water.

162
00:08:19.625 --> 00:08:22.000
The more desperate,
the more expensive.

163
00:08:22.083 --> 00:08:22.958
-How much?

164
00:08:23.667 --> 00:08:25.000
[Owen sighs]

165
00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:26.958
-Probably a 100 grand.

166
00:08:27.042 --> 00:08:28.042
[tender score]

167
00:08:30.125 --> 00:08:31.708
I'm sorry, I'm doing all I can.

168
00:08:31.792 --> 00:08:33.250
It's just that it--

169
00:08:41.667 --> 00:08:43.875
I'll get a crew together
if you guys can get the money.

170
00:08:44.958 --> 00:08:45.958
-Okay.

171
00:08:46.833 --> 00:08:47.833
Do what you can.

172
00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:51.417
This place is gonna die
without water, man.

173
00:08:52.292 --> 00:08:53.208
[ominous score]

174
00:08:55.375 --> 00:08:56.750
-[in Chinese]
The weather conditions are
clear.

175
00:08:58.292 --> 00:09:01.042
-[in Chinese] Let them know
we'll arrive at the Green Zone
in two groups.

176
00:09:01.125 --> 00:09:02.792
One at nine a.m., the
second at four p.m.

177
00:09:02.875 --> 00:09:03.958
-[in Chinese] Got it.

178
00:09:04.042 --> 00:09:05.250
-English, please.

179
00:09:05.708 --> 00:09:06.875
<i><font color="white">What about air recon?</font></i>

180
00:09:07.458 --> 00:09:10.000
-Your primary and secondary
routes to the Green Zone are
hostile.

181
00:09:10.083 --> 00:09:12.833
-[Pilot] <i><font color="white">Sir, all the other</font></i>
<i><font color="white">options are rebel controlled.</font></i>

182
00:09:12.917 --> 00:09:13.917
[comm clicks off]

183
00:09:14.708 --> 00:09:17.167
-Then we're still taking
the Highway of Death.

184
00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:18.500
It's the fastest way

185
00:09:19.042 --> 00:09:20.292
from here to the Green Zone.

186
00:09:20.375 --> 00:09:21.833
Nonstop, eight hours.

187
00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:23.417
[dramatic score]

188
00:09:32.708 --> 00:09:33.542
[tender score]

189
00:09:34.333 --> 00:09:35.375
-Chris,

190
00:09:36.208 --> 00:09:39.000
where are we going
to get the $100,000?

191
00:09:39.625 --> 00:09:40.458
[sighs]

192
00:09:40.542 --> 00:09:41.875
-[crickets chirping]
-[dog barking in distance]

193
00:09:42.458 --> 00:09:43.458
-I'll think of something.

194
00:09:44.417 --> 00:09:45.250
-Okay.

195
00:09:47.208 --> 00:09:48.500
[receding footsteps]

196
00:09:54.792 --> 00:09:55.625
[object clatters to table]

197
00:09:56.250 --> 00:09:57.333
[dramatic score]

198
00:09:59.667 --> 00:10:00.750
-Sector four, ready.

199
00:10:00.833 --> 00:10:02.125
-Sector three, ready.

200
00:10:02.208 --> 00:10:03.250
[beeping]

201
00:10:03.583 --> 00:10:04.500
-Sector two, ready.

202
00:10:04.583 --> 00:10:05.958
-Sector one, ready.

203
00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:09.167
-[in Chinese] We
are shutting down.

204
00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:10.250
-[in Chinese] Got it.

205
00:10:13.167 --> 00:10:15.625
-[in Chinese]
Professor, we need the dongle.

206
00:10:16.625 --> 00:10:17.542
[whirring]

207
00:10:19.042 --> 00:10:20.042
[slow rhythmic beeping]

208
00:10:23.417 --> 00:10:24.000
[two quick beeps]

209
00:10:26.042 --> 00:10:27.667
[machinery whirring down]

210
00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:30.500
-[in Chinese] You
feeling better?

211
00:10:31.708 --> 00:10:32.667
-[in Chinese] Not really.

212
00:10:33.250 --> 00:10:34.167
[metal ratcheting]

213
00:10:36.417 --> 00:10:37.333
[prolonged beep]

214
00:10:38.167 --> 00:10:39.042
[in Chinese] System off.

215
00:10:40.583 --> 00:10:42.708
-[in Chinese] Mei, hold my bag
for me. -[in Chinese] Okay.

216
00:10:42.792 --> 00:10:44.042
-[in Chinese] Be careful.

217
00:10:46.167 --> 00:10:48.458
-[in Chinese]
Professor, we must go right
away.

218
00:10:49.125 --> 00:10:51.000
-[Cheng in Chinese]
Get ready, everyone, we're
going!

219
00:10:51.083 --> 00:10:51.958
[nervous chatter]

220
00:10:54.292 --> 00:10:55.083
[dramatic score]

221
00:10:58.458 --> 00:11:00.417
-[in Chinese] Do a head count.
-[in Chinese] Yes, sir.

222
00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:01.500
-Come on.

223
00:11:01.583 --> 00:11:02.500
[children chattering]

224
00:11:03.167 --> 00:11:03.917
Follow me.

225
00:11:04.708 --> 00:11:05.792
Come on, come on.

226
00:11:08.542 --> 00:11:12.333
-[in Chinese] Professor,
there's still another seat on
bus eight.

227
00:11:12.417 --> 00:11:14.333
You can go with your assistant.

228
00:11:14.417 --> 00:11:16.208
-[in Chinese]
Excellent. Let's go.

229
00:11:16.292 --> 00:11:17.875
-[in Chinese] But
you are on bus one.

230
00:11:18.542 --> 00:11:19.792
[soldier shouting]

231
00:11:21.083 --> 00:11:22.083
-[in Chinese] Okay.

232
00:11:22.167 --> 00:11:23.333
I'll see you in the Green Zone.

233
00:11:23.417 --> 00:11:24.625
-[in Chinese] Please be careful.

234
00:11:29.125 --> 00:11:30.125
[cap clicking off
spray paint can]

235
00:11:30.792 --> 00:11:31.792
[hissing]

236
00:11:40.167 --> 00:11:41.250
-[in Chinese] Dr. Mei.

237
00:11:41.958 --> 00:11:43.042
I saved a seat for you.

238
00:11:51.042 --> 00:11:52.125
Shadow Squad.

239
00:11:55.792 --> 00:11:56.833
Let's go!

240
00:11:56.917 --> 00:11:57.917
-[in Chinese] Yes, sir.

241
00:12:09.458 --> 00:12:10.458
-[in Chinese] Move out.

242
00:12:10.958 --> 00:12:11.833
You hold tight.

243
00:12:12.292 --> 00:12:14.042
-[pilot] Okay, let's go.

244
00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:16.167
[helicopter blades thumping]

245
00:12:18.833 --> 00:12:19.667
[engines whining]

246
00:12:30.833 --> 00:12:32.000
-Commander Luo,

247
00:12:32.583 --> 00:12:34.833
the helicopters are pushing
ahead to the Green Zone.

248
00:12:35.875 --> 00:12:37.000
You're on your own now.

249
00:12:44.667 --> 00:12:45.542
[beep]

250
00:12:49.250 --> 00:12:50.458
-Radio check one.

251
00:12:50.542 --> 00:12:51.542
<i><font color="white">-Two check.</font></i>

252
00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:53.458
<i><font color="white">-Three check.</font></i>

253
00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:54.708
<i><font color="white">-Four check.</font></i>

254
00:12:56.083 --> 00:12:56.792
<i><font color="white">-Five check.</font></i>

255
00:12:57.583 --> 00:12:58.333
<i><font color="white">-Six check.</font></i>

256
00:12:59.542 --> 00:13:00.375
<i><font color="white">-Seven check.</font></i>

257
00:13:00.792 --> 00:13:01.708
<i><font color="white">-Eight check.</font></i>

258
00:13:02.208 --> 00:13:02.875
<i><font color="white">-Nine check.</font></i>

259
00:13:03.708 --> 00:13:04.542
<i><font color="white">-Ten check.</font></i>

260
00:13:05.167 --> 00:13:06.042
<i><font color="white">-Eleven check.</font></i>

261
00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:07.958
[click]

262
00:13:11.625 --> 00:13:12.667
[metal creaks, clangs]

263
00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:13.750
[diary hits seat]

264
00:13:16.417 --> 00:13:17.625
[gasps]

265
00:13:21.208 --> 00:13:22.750
-[in Chinese]
You can't stand the whole way.

266
00:13:22.833 --> 00:13:24.208
Road's bumpy, it's dangerous.

267
00:13:25.750 --> 00:13:26.875
-[in Chinese] I'm fine.

268
00:13:30.500 --> 00:13:32.583
-[in Chinese] More
stubborn than your mom.

269
00:13:35.708 --> 00:13:37.708
-[in Chinese] So you
still remember her?

270
00:13:49.333 --> 00:13:50.333
[engine slows]

271
00:13:51.167 --> 00:13:52.250
[air brakes hiss]

272
00:13:52.333 --> 00:13:53.333
[ominous score]

273
00:14:03.667 --> 00:14:05.042
The Highway of Death.

274
00:14:05.833 --> 00:14:06.875
It looks so tragic.

275
00:14:09.417 --> 00:14:11.375
-[in Chinese] A lot of people
died here during the war.

276
00:14:11.458 --> 00:14:12.875
It's still dangerous here.

277
00:14:13.542 --> 00:14:14.583
Don't worry, we'll be okay.

278
00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:17.500
Watch the sides.

279
00:14:17.917 --> 00:14:18.917
Prepare yourselves.

280
00:14:22.625 --> 00:14:23.625
Please sit down.

281
00:14:24.125 --> 00:14:25.125
Hm?

282
00:14:26.125 --> 00:14:27.083
[Mei scoffs]

283
00:14:32.917 --> 00:14:33.917
Seatbelt please.

284
00:14:37.208 --> 00:14:38.250
[air brakes hiss]

285
00:14:38.333 --> 00:14:39.208
[gear selector ratchets]

286
00:14:39.292 --> 00:14:40.125
[engine revving]

287
00:14:40.625 --> 00:14:41.792
[gear selector ratchets]

288
00:14:41.875 --> 00:14:42.958
[exciting score]

289
00:14:59.917 --> 00:15:01.083
-[in Chinese] There's
a minefield ahead.

290
00:15:02.542 --> 00:15:03.625
-[in Arabic] I can
see them coming!

291
00:15:06.167 --> 00:15:07.458
-[in Chinese] I
know. Don't worry.

292
00:15:09.417 --> 00:15:11.208
Stay in formation. Be careful.

293
00:15:14.125 --> 00:15:15.417
-[in Chinese] What
are you doing?

294
00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:16.833
-[in Chinese] There's
no mines there.

295
00:15:17.583 --> 00:15:18.333
[condor screeches]

296
00:15:23.458 --> 00:15:24.458
[tires squealing]

297
00:15:33.792 --> 00:15:34.750
[explosion]

298
00:15:35.667 --> 00:15:36.667
[excited chatter]

299
00:15:37.917 --> 00:15:38.917
[dramatic score]

300
00:15:41.167 --> 00:15:42.208
[excited chatter]

301
00:16:01.458 --> 00:16:02.542
You see?

302
00:16:03.667 --> 00:16:04.667
It's all a trap.

303
00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:06.500
They want to lure you in

304
00:16:07.917 --> 00:16:09.875
somewhere you think is safe
and take your life.

305
00:16:30.333 --> 00:16:31.333
Mei,

306
00:16:32.750 --> 00:16:35.000
I'm here to protect you.

307
00:16:35.958 --> 00:16:38.167
-[in Chinese]
You are here to be a hero not
for me,

308
00:16:39.500 --> 00:16:40.542
but for them.

309
00:16:42.833 --> 00:16:44.958
-[in Chinese]
Your name was on the evacuation
list.

310
00:16:48.417 --> 00:16:49.250
[unbuckles seatbelt]

311
00:16:51.375 --> 00:16:52.375
-[in Chinese] So,

312
00:16:53.292 --> 00:16:55.667
you brought your team
all the way here to save me

313
00:16:56.375 --> 00:16:57.500
just for my forgiveness?

314
00:16:58.042 --> 00:16:59.042
It's not gonna happen.

315
00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:01.208
You broke my mom's heart.

316
00:17:01.667 --> 00:17:02.708
And mine as well.

317
00:17:02.792 --> 00:17:04.125
I'll never forgive you.

318
00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:06.625
-[in Chinese] It was your mom
who took you away from me.

319
00:17:06.708 --> 00:17:09.167
-[in Chinese] That's just
because you never cared about
us.

320
00:17:10.333 --> 00:17:12.333
My mom was lying
there in the hospital,

321
00:17:13.917 --> 00:17:15.667
she couldn't get out of bed

322
00:17:16.458 --> 00:17:19.250
but you never bothered to visit
her, not even once.

323
00:17:24.167 --> 00:17:25.667
How could you be so cruel?

324
00:17:26.667 --> 00:17:28.917
-[in Chinese]
I was on a top secret mission.

325
00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:30.000
Our country needed me.

326
00:17:30.875 --> 00:17:31.833
-[in Chinese] Our
country needed you?

327
00:17:32.625 --> 00:17:33.625
Right.

328
00:17:35.542 --> 00:17:36.375
What about me?

329
00:17:37.208 --> 00:17:38.750
I was so little.

330
00:17:39.375 --> 00:17:42.208
Mom was in the hospital,
she needed you more.

331
00:17:47.083 --> 00:17:48.583
But what have you done for us?

332
00:17:58.000 --> 00:17:59.250
As an engineer here,

333
00:18:00.292 --> 00:18:01.292
I'm grateful for you.

334
00:18:02.375 --> 00:18:03.375
But as your daughter,

335
00:18:05.167 --> 00:18:06.167
there's nothing left to say.

336
00:18:10.708 --> 00:18:12.250
-[in Chinese] Dragon,
on your one o'clock.

337
00:18:14.250 --> 00:18:15.250
[dramatic score continues]

338
00:18:19.292 --> 00:18:20.625
-[in Chinese]
Attention, everybody.

339
00:18:21.333 --> 00:18:22.583
There's a sandstorm up ahead.

340
00:18:28.667 --> 00:18:29.500
QiXing,

341
00:18:29.583 --> 00:18:31.417
didn't you say the
weather was clear?

342
00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:33.333
-[in Chinese]
I've been keeping an eye on the
data.

343
00:18:33.417 --> 00:18:35.542
It shows
the chance of a sandstorm here
is zero.

344
00:18:35.625 --> 00:18:38.042
-[Luo in Chinese] If we don't
keep going, we'll miss our
window.

345
00:18:38.125 --> 00:18:39.583
Jing and Yan, close the hatches.

346
00:18:39.667 --> 00:18:41.750
We need to get through
as fast as possible.

347
00:18:47.333 --> 00:18:48.375
[dramatic score continues]

348
00:19:00.375 --> 00:19:01.125
[soft boom]

349
00:19:06.250 --> 00:19:08.750
This sandstorm is very unusual.

350
00:19:09.875 --> 00:19:10.875
[ominous score]

351
00:19:12.333 --> 00:19:13.333
HaiMing.

352
00:19:15.625 --> 00:19:16.625
HaiMing?

353
00:19:18.625 --> 00:19:19.625
HaiMing, do you copy?

354
00:19:20.708 --> 00:19:22.458
-[in Chinese] I
don't copy either.

355
00:19:23.417 --> 00:19:24.083
-[in Chinese] ShenWei?

356
00:19:24.708 --> 00:19:25.708
Yan?

357
00:19:27.833 --> 00:19:29.375
Strange, there is no signal.

358
00:19:29.875 --> 00:19:31.417
-[in Chinese] Hey, is that--

359
00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:33.125
-[Luo in Chinese] What?

360
00:19:35.125 --> 00:19:36.125
-[in Chinese] Huh?

361
00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:38.708
Nothing. I thought
I saw something.

362
00:19:41.292 --> 00:19:42.542
[engines revving loudly]

363
00:19:45.292 --> 00:19:46.500
-[Chris] Should be
close to the target.

364
00:19:46.583 --> 00:19:47.708
Tell me what you see.

365
00:19:48.833 --> 00:19:49.875
-[Henry] There it is.

366
00:19:50.833 --> 00:19:52.500
Our objective plus
four of her core crew.

367
00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:55.583
-[Chris] Toothpick, Tomb Raider,
we're on the X.

368
00:19:55.667 --> 00:19:57.667
Scribblehead, extract
and drop. Let's go.

369
00:19:57.750 --> 00:19:58.708
[loud engines]

370
00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:01.458
-My name is Knox.

371
00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:03.167
[engine revving]

372
00:20:05.833 --> 00:20:06.917
[clicking]

373
00:20:09.417 --> 00:20:11.333
-[in Chinese] How is it
causing so much interference?

374
00:20:11.417 --> 00:20:12.458
[engine revving]

375
00:20:15.708 --> 00:20:16.625
[frightened exclamations]

376
00:20:20.708 --> 00:20:21.458
[engine accelerating]

377
00:20:21.542 --> 00:20:22.833
Get back on the main road.

378
00:20:27.417 --> 00:20:28.708
-[Chris] You having fun yet?

379
00:20:28.792 --> 00:20:30.250
Just keep your head on a swivel.

380
00:20:31.583 --> 00:20:32.875
[compressed air
releasing suddenly]

381
00:20:35.667 --> 00:20:36.625
[tires squealing]

382
00:20:45.125 --> 00:20:46.042
[rapid beeping]

383
00:20:52.125 --> 00:20:53.208
[driver exclaims]

384
00:20:58.125 --> 00:20:59.208
[boom]

385
00:20:59.292 --> 00:21:00.375
[screams and cries]

386
00:21:01.792 --> 00:21:02.583
[grunt]

387
00:21:03.583 --> 00:21:04.375
[dramatic score]

388
00:21:05.250 --> 00:21:06.125
[boom]

389
00:21:06.792 --> 00:21:07.625
-[Henry] Everybody down!

390
00:21:07.708 --> 00:21:08.792
Nobody move!

391
00:21:08.875 --> 00:21:09.917
On the ground!

392
00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:10.875
You, got a hearing problem?

393
00:21:10.958 --> 00:21:11.917
[grunt]

394
00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:13.250
On the floor, don't move!

395
00:21:13.333 --> 00:21:14.458
On the ground!

396
00:21:14.542 --> 00:21:16.292
-[Chris] All clear. Lane secure.

397
00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:20.042
-Down, down, get down.

398
00:21:20.125 --> 00:21:21.042
You, wanna die?

399
00:21:21.917 --> 00:21:23.292
On the floor! Don't move.

400
00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:25.833
[gunshots]

401
00:21:25.917 --> 00:21:26.917
[passengers screaming]

402
00:21:27.792 --> 00:21:28.792
[gunshots]

403
00:21:30.542 --> 00:21:31.375
[grunts, groans]

404
00:21:47.750 --> 00:21:48.750
[knife singing]

405
00:21:55.958 --> 00:21:56.917
[thud, grunt]

406
00:21:57.542 --> 00:21:58.500
[tinkling]

407
00:21:59.583 --> 00:22:00.458
[grunt]

408
00:22:00.542 --> 00:22:01.542
[bus engine revving]

409
00:22:03.917 --> 00:22:04.750
[excited chatter]

410
00:22:05.875 --> 00:22:06.917
[grunt]
[thud]

411
00:22:12.833 --> 00:22:13.917
[tires screeching]

412
00:22:18.417 --> 00:22:19.292
[tires screeching]

413
00:22:21.458 --> 00:22:22.583
-[in Chinese] Where
are they going?

414
00:22:27.833 --> 00:22:29.208
[digital clicks, interference]

415
00:22:29.917 --> 00:22:30.917
-[in Chinese] Strange…

416
00:22:33.792 --> 00:22:34.792
[nervous chatter]

417
00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:40.708
ShenWei?

418
00:22:40.792 --> 00:22:42.083
Yan, HaiMing?

419
00:22:42.167 --> 00:22:43.167
Does anyone copy?

420
00:22:44.333 --> 00:22:45.333
[air brakes hiss]

421
00:22:48.417 --> 00:22:49.417
[dramatic score]

422
00:22:50.792 --> 00:22:51.792
Gather round!

423
00:22:53.542 --> 00:22:54.542
-[in Chinese] Hurry up!

424
00:22:57.042 --> 00:22:58.417
-[in Chinese] Why
isn't anyone answering?

425
00:22:58.500 --> 00:23:00.458
-[in Chinese] Our comms
went completely down just now.

426
00:23:00.542 --> 00:23:01.792
-[in Chinese] What
about you guys?

427
00:23:01.875 --> 00:23:03.375
-[in Chinese] There's
nothing. No signal.

428
00:23:04.333 --> 00:23:05.375
-[in Chinese] Are
all the buses here?

429
00:23:05.458 --> 00:23:07.125
-[in Chinese]
I saw bus eight leave the
convoy.

430
00:23:07.208 --> 00:23:08.083
-[in Chinese] Where did it go?

431
00:23:08.167 --> 00:23:08.958
-[in Chinese] East.

432
00:23:11.500 --> 00:23:13.208
-[in Chinese] Where is Yan?
-[in Chinese] Bus 11 is gone too.

433
00:23:13.292 --> 00:23:14.542
-[in Chinese] What's
wrong with you?

434
00:23:14.625 --> 00:23:16.583
You lost two entire
buses in a sandstorm.

435
00:23:19.250 --> 00:23:21.125
-[in Chinese] That
storm is not natural.

436
00:23:21.208 --> 00:23:22.458
[score swells, fades out]

437
00:23:22.542 --> 00:23:24.208
-[in Chinese] Hurry
up, hurry up, go!

438
00:23:26.042 --> 00:23:27.500
Go. Go.

439
00:23:29.083 --> 00:23:31.042
-Hey, these the guys
that armed Area Seven?

440
00:23:31.125 --> 00:23:32.250
-Yeah, why?
-These guys?

441
00:23:32.333 --> 00:23:33.292
[Henry scoffs quietly]

442
00:23:33.375 --> 00:23:35.250
-What's a criminal
supposed to look like, bro, huh?

443
00:23:35.333 --> 00:23:36.750
You remember Typhoid Mary?

444
00:23:36.833 --> 00:23:38.000
She killed like a 100 people.

445
00:23:38.542 --> 00:23:39.833
Yeah, she was just a cook.

446
00:23:41.542 --> 00:23:42.792
[beeping]

447
00:23:43.500 --> 00:23:44.500
-[in Chinese] We got it!

448
00:23:45.042 --> 00:23:46.292
-[in Chinese] Dragon!

449
00:23:47.292 --> 00:23:49.583
-Captain Azir, we
lost two buses.

450
00:23:49.667 --> 00:23:51.333
<i><font color="white">We need both helicopters here.</font></i>

451
00:23:51.417 --> 00:23:52.667
-Copy, Commander.

452
00:23:52.750 --> 00:23:54.208
We are circling back.

453
00:23:54.292 --> 00:23:55.292
-Okay.

454
00:23:55.833 --> 00:23:57.125
-[in Chinese] Take the second helicopter. 
-[in Chinese] Okay.

455
00:23:57.208 --> 00:23:58.708
-[in Chinese] Follow me.
-[in Chinese] Where?

456
00:23:58.792 --> 00:24:00.083
-[in Chinese]
You're familiar with this
desert.

457
00:24:00.167 --> 00:24:01.917
Isn't this part of your job?

458
00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:02.833
-[in Chinese] Yeah,

459
00:24:02.917 --> 00:24:04.500
I have surveyed this area
with Professor Cheng before.

460
00:24:04.583 --> 00:24:05.500
Why?

461
00:24:05.583 --> 00:24:07.583
-[in Chinese] I need your help
finding the missing buses.

462
00:24:07.667 --> 00:24:08.667
-[in Chinese] I…

463
00:24:09.125 --> 00:24:10.042
[dramatic score]

464
00:24:11.875 --> 00:24:13.333
-[in Chinese]
Don't worry, I will protect you.

465
00:24:15.042 --> 00:24:15.833
[helicopter blades whirring]

466
00:24:20.667 --> 00:24:21.750
[dramatic score continues]

467
00:24:45.500 --> 00:24:46.667
-It's breaking up.

468
00:24:47.917 --> 00:24:49.750
-This doesn't happen
in the canyons.

469
00:24:49.833 --> 00:24:50.833
-Look!

470
00:24:52.292 --> 00:24:53.292
[wind blowing]

471
00:25:03.042 --> 00:25:03.917
[in Chinese] ShenWei,

472
00:25:04.000 --> 00:25:05.583
the sandstorm was man-made.

473
00:25:06.583 --> 00:25:09.625
They used jet engines
to push the sand.

474
00:25:10.375 --> 00:25:11.292
-[in Chinese]<i><font color="white"> Copy.</font></i>

475
00:25:11.375 --> 00:25:12.375
-Azir,

476
00:25:12.917 --> 00:25:14.042
head north.

477
00:25:18.792 --> 00:25:19.792
[exciting score]

478
00:25:26.167 --> 00:25:27.375
-[in Chinese] Dragon, Dragon!

479
00:25:28.625 --> 00:25:29.375
Dragon!

480
00:25:30.250 --> 00:25:31.250
Can you hear me?

481
00:25:32.375 --> 00:25:34.250
We were ambushed by mercenaries.

482
00:25:34.333 --> 00:25:35.583
-[in Chinese] Who were they?

483
00:25:35.667 --> 00:25:37.500
-[in Chinese] Americans.
They were very fast.

484
00:25:38.167 --> 00:25:39.000
Very organized.

485
00:25:39.667 --> 00:25:40.917
-[in Chinese] You stand down.

486
00:25:42.042 --> 00:25:43.833
Connect with HaiMing.

487
00:25:44.500 --> 00:25:45.417
-[in Chinese] Copy.

488
00:25:51.417 --> 00:25:52.292
-[in Chinese] HaiMing,

489
00:25:52.708 --> 00:25:55.042
can you get a GPS
position on bus eight?

490
00:25:56.083 --> 00:25:58.083
-[in Chinese] GPS
can't locate it.

491
00:25:58.167 --> 00:25:59.167
-[in Chinese] ShenWei,

492
00:25:59.750 --> 00:26:01.292
scan a 10-mile radius

493
00:26:01.917 --> 00:26:03.833
for any fast-moving vehicles.

494
00:26:03.917 --> 00:26:05.917
Report if you find anything.

495
00:26:06.792 --> 00:26:07.792
-[in Chinese] Copy.

496
00:26:08.792 --> 00:26:09.875
[in English] Circle around.

497
00:26:10.750 --> 00:26:11.750
[engine revving]

498
00:26:21.917 --> 00:26:22.875
-What's your problem?

499
00:26:22.958 --> 00:26:24.375
-I knew I couldn't trust you.

500
00:26:25.250 --> 00:26:26.958
-Bro, you are paranoid.

501
00:26:27.542 --> 00:26:29.208
-Shit. Incoming!

502
00:26:29.292 --> 00:26:30.375
[helicopter blades thumping]

503
00:26:33.333 --> 00:26:34.333
Cover fire.

504
00:26:35.042 --> 00:26:36.917
-Must be them! Go, go, go.

505
00:26:37.000 --> 00:26:37.667
-Copy!

506
00:26:46.542 --> 00:26:47.542
[dramatic score]

507
00:26:51.167 --> 00:26:52.167
[gunshots]

508
00:26:52.667 --> 00:26:53.458
-[in Chinese] Dragon Luo,

509
00:26:53.542 --> 00:26:57.000
there's suspicious mercenaries
and they're firing on us!

510
00:26:58.833 --> 00:27:00.458
-Let's go. Head east.

511
00:27:01.667 --> 00:27:02.667
[in Chinese] Yan,

512
00:27:03.042 --> 00:27:05.083
join up with the rest of the
team and head to the Green Zone.

513
00:27:05.667 --> 00:27:07.125
I'll meet you there.

514
00:27:07.208 --> 00:27:07.958
-[in Chinese] Copy.

515
00:27:08.042 --> 00:27:09.000
-[in Chinese] HaiMing,

516
00:27:09.083 --> 00:27:10.333
get the convoy rolling.

517
00:27:11.250 --> 00:27:12.042
-[in Chinese] Copy.

518
00:27:20.250 --> 00:27:21.250
[engine revving]

519
00:27:26.083 --> 00:27:27.125
[gunshot]

520
00:27:29.292 --> 00:27:30.417
[beeping]

521
00:27:40.708 --> 00:27:41.708
[whizzing]

522
00:27:54.292 --> 00:27:55.542
[engines revving]

523
00:27:55.625 --> 00:27:56.708
-I just lost my lead.

524
00:27:56.792 --> 00:27:58.208
Etch-a-Sketch, you're up,
you take point.

525
00:27:58.292 --> 00:27:59.333
-It's Knox!

526
00:28:08.917 --> 00:28:09.958
[heavy weapon firing]

527
00:28:12.333 --> 00:28:14.583
-Cyclops, push ahead
and set up an ambush.

528
00:28:14.667 --> 00:28:16.167
-My name is Knox!

529
00:28:25.042 --> 00:28:25.875
Shit!

530
00:28:25.958 --> 00:28:27.250
[heavy weapon firing]

531
00:28:33.750 --> 00:28:35.000
He's moving too fast.

532
00:28:37.042 --> 00:28:37.958
-Hold on!

533
00:28:38.042 --> 00:28:39.083
[boom]

534
00:28:42.958 --> 00:28:44.500
Tomb Raider, cover me now.

535
00:28:44.583 --> 00:28:46.333
Tramp Stamp, I'm
drawing this helo away

536
00:28:46.417 --> 00:28:48.042
and you stay behind
and take it out!

537
00:28:49.125 --> 00:28:50.292
[tires skidding]

538
00:28:54.583 --> 00:28:56.167
-We need to keep going.

539
00:28:56.250 --> 00:28:58.250
-We got no chance
with that thing in the air.

540
00:29:02.458 --> 00:29:03.792
-You take care of the bird.

541
00:29:03.875 --> 00:29:05.333
I'll get 'em to
the exchange site.

542
00:29:05.417 --> 00:29:06.458
-Copy!

543
00:29:11.833 --> 00:29:12.583
Set.

544
00:29:17.583 --> 00:29:19.667
Tramp Stamp, take it out.

545
00:29:19.750 --> 00:29:21.125
[helicopter blades whirring]

546
00:29:29.500 --> 00:29:30.250
-I'm out.

547
00:29:32.250 --> 00:29:33.042
[rapid beeping]

548
00:29:33.125 --> 00:29:34.458
-[Tomb Raider] I'm out.

549
00:29:37.375 --> 00:29:38.208
-We're clear.

550
00:29:40.917 --> 00:29:42.708
Goddammit, Knox, take your shot!

551
00:29:43.792 --> 00:29:44.792
[rapid beeping]

552
00:29:52.500 --> 00:29:53.417
-I got it.

553
00:29:53.500 --> 00:29:54.417
-[in Chinese] We're going down.

554
00:29:57.917 --> 00:29:58.958
[engine revving]

555
00:30:02.500 --> 00:30:03.500
[engine idling]

556
00:30:03.583 --> 00:30:04.583
[dramatic score]

557
00:30:07.958 --> 00:30:09.042
[engine revving]

558
00:30:44.333 --> 00:30:45.333
-Commander.

559
00:30:46.917 --> 00:30:47.917
Look.

560
00:30:50.708 --> 00:30:51.917
-Go!

561
00:30:56.875 --> 00:30:57.875
[wind howling]

562
00:31:04.292 --> 00:31:05.417
-[in Chinese] You're
going down like this?

563
00:31:06.583 --> 00:31:07.708
Be careful.

564
00:31:40.333 --> 00:31:41.333
[frightened exclamations]

565
00:31:41.417 --> 00:31:42.667
[dramatic score]

566
00:31:45.875 --> 00:31:46.875
Five.

567
00:31:46.958 --> 00:31:47.958
-[in Chinese] Wei.

568
00:31:48.333 --> 00:31:49.042
-[in Chinese] Dragon Luo,

569
00:31:49.125 --> 00:31:50.542
they took five people with them.

570
00:31:51.292 --> 00:31:53.167
-Azir, five missing.

571
00:31:53.750 --> 00:31:54.792
I need Mei down here.

572
00:31:56.083 --> 00:31:57.083
-[Henry] What's going on?

573
00:31:57.833 --> 00:31:58.833
-Who hired us?

574
00:31:59.708 --> 00:32:01.250
-Unicorp.
-Don't lie to me, Henry!

575
00:32:01.333 --> 00:32:02.292
What are you mixed up in?

576
00:32:02.375 --> 00:32:04.417
-Go easy on him, Chris.

577
00:32:07.750 --> 00:32:08.750
[dramatic score]

578
00:32:09.542 --> 00:32:10.625
It's like you said,

579
00:32:11.292 --> 00:32:13.042
no one works harder than me.

580
00:32:13.125 --> 00:32:14.250
-Owen?

581
00:32:15.375 --> 00:32:16.208
[Owen laughing]

582
00:32:18.042 --> 00:32:19.042
[helicopter blades thumping]

583
00:32:21.917 --> 00:32:22.917
[excited chatter]

584
00:32:25.875 --> 00:32:26.833
-[in Chinese] Hey, Mei,

585
00:32:27.125 --> 00:32:28.958
they took Professor Cheng
and her assistant.

586
00:32:29.042 --> 00:32:30.042
-[in Chinese] What?

587
00:32:36.417 --> 00:32:37.458
[Cheng gasps]

588
00:32:37.917 --> 00:32:39.542
-Professor Ying Cheng.

589
00:32:40.958 --> 00:32:41.958
Finally.

590
00:32:42.500 --> 00:32:44.583
I'm very, very thankful
you could make it.

591
00:32:46.958 --> 00:32:48.000
-Have we met?

592
00:32:48.417 --> 00:32:50.958
-No, I'm afraid
I haven't had the pleasure until
now.

593
00:32:51.917 --> 00:32:54.500
I hope my men
didn't cause too many problems
for you.

594
00:32:56.667 --> 00:32:59.083
-It was you attacking
our refinery?

595
00:33:00.250 --> 00:33:01.833
-Please understand, professor,

596
00:33:02.333 --> 00:33:03.583
it's not personal.

597
00:33:04.958 --> 00:33:06.000
Knox!

598
00:33:09.833 --> 00:33:10.792
Let's talk.

599
00:33:11.625 --> 00:33:12.625
[indistinct chatter]

600
00:33:13.583 --> 00:33:15.000
I've been all over this country.

601
00:33:18.250 --> 00:33:19.458
You know what I've found?

602
00:33:22.208 --> 00:33:23.208
This isn't a desert.

603
00:33:24.292 --> 00:33:26.000
Everything here is a gold mine.

604
00:33:26.833 --> 00:33:28.708
And I'm wiping the
company out, Chris.

605
00:33:29.208 --> 00:33:30.208
-What?

606
00:33:31.833 --> 00:33:34.375
-I watched them get rich
while I busted my ass off.

607
00:33:35.583 --> 00:33:37.667
Sixteen years of false promises.

608
00:33:39.583 --> 00:33:40.625
[sighs]

609
00:33:40.708 --> 00:33:42.458
I even gave up having
a family for them.

610
00:33:43.750 --> 00:33:44.750
And for what?

611
00:33:46.292 --> 00:33:47.292
Nothing.

612
00:33:49.083 --> 00:33:50.167
But now it's my turn.

613
00:33:52.250 --> 00:33:53.542
I'm taking this war private.

614
00:33:53.625 --> 00:33:55.083
I'm taking back
what they owe me.

615
00:33:55.625 --> 00:33:56.625
What they owe us.

616
00:33:56.708 --> 00:33:58.625
-Listen, Owen, what you got
going on here that's your
business.

617
00:33:59.208 --> 00:34:00.458
It's between you and her.

618
00:34:01.583 --> 00:34:02.583
-Hm.

619
00:34:04.292 --> 00:34:06.958
Dragon Luo is leading
the Chinese security team.

620
00:34:08.083 --> 00:34:09.875
He's gonna come
after the professor.

621
00:34:10.750 --> 00:34:13.583
If you can keep him off my tail,
I can make you rich.

622
00:34:13.667 --> 00:34:15.292
-Not interested.
I just want my money.

623
00:34:15.375 --> 00:34:16.375
-When the job is done.

624
00:34:16.458 --> 00:34:18.250
-The job is done.
Henry said dropping--

625
00:34:18.333 --> 00:34:19.833
-Henry's young and desperate!

626
00:34:22.292 --> 00:34:25.042
You can't trust people
who are desperate.

627
00:34:31.500 --> 00:34:32.542
It's our time.

628
00:34:34.292 --> 00:34:36.417
You don't want to pass
this up, my friend.

629
00:34:36.875 --> 00:34:38.000
And remember,

630
00:34:38.958 --> 00:34:39.958
no money,

631
00:34:40.333 --> 00:34:41.333
no water.

632
00:34:42.292 --> 00:34:43.542
-Selfish son of a bitch.

633
00:34:44.250 --> 00:34:45.250
-I'm selfish?

634
00:34:45.833 --> 00:34:47.000
[dramatic score]

635
00:34:49.708 --> 00:34:51.292
You know what selfish is?

636
00:34:52.042 --> 00:34:53.208
Staying here and hiding.

637
00:34:56.125 --> 00:34:57.083
-I'm done with you.

638
00:34:57.167 --> 00:34:58.083
-Whatever you want.

639
00:34:58.667 --> 00:35:00.625
-Whoa, whoa, whoa,
you're just gonna let him walk?

640
00:35:00.708 --> 00:35:01.708
-He's your brother.

641
00:35:02.333 --> 00:35:03.333
You stop him.

642
00:35:04.792 --> 00:35:06.083
-Chris, wait.

643
00:35:06.708 --> 00:35:08.708
I-I need to collect our money
and we gotta finish.

644
00:35:08.792 --> 00:35:10.125
-Get out of here
while you still can.

645
00:35:10.208 --> 00:35:11.292
[engine starts, rumbles]

646
00:35:12.167 --> 00:35:13.250
-Well, go on then.

647
00:35:13.958 --> 00:35:14.792
Quit.

648
00:35:16.417 --> 00:35:18.708
Just like you did
when you bailed on our old man.

649
00:35:19.292 --> 00:35:20.417
[engine revving]

650
00:35:20.500 --> 00:35:22.042
-Be at the village
at 1600 sharp.

651
00:35:22.125 --> 00:35:24.333
Bring the rest of my money
and don't be late.

652
00:35:24.417 --> 00:35:25.417
[revs engine]

653
00:35:25.792 --> 00:35:26.792
[tires skidding]

654
00:35:32.292 --> 00:35:33.292
-Owen.

655
00:35:33.917 --> 00:35:34.792
We don't need him.

656
00:35:35.875 --> 00:35:38.125
I can handle this
Dragon Luo guy on my own.

657
00:35:39.542 --> 00:35:40.750
-You failed, Henry.

658
00:35:40.833 --> 00:35:42.375
That makes me so sad.

659
00:35:42.458 --> 00:35:43.833
[dramatic score]

660
00:35:43.917 --> 00:35:45.208
[metallic ting]

661
00:35:51.000 --> 00:35:51.917
[grunts]

662
00:35:54.292 --> 00:35:55.167
Stop!

663
00:35:56.167 --> 00:35:57.208
We need the hostages.

664
00:35:59.542 --> 00:36:00.542
Idiot.

665
00:36:09.083 --> 00:36:11.042
Take him back to the radio tower

666
00:36:11.125 --> 00:36:13.333
and make it look like
Chinese payback, okay?

667
00:36:13.417 --> 00:36:16.125
Also, close the loop
on Henry's bullshit with the
French.

668
00:36:16.208 --> 00:36:18.167
We can't have them
interfering with the plan.

669
00:36:18.750 --> 00:36:19.583
Let's go!

670
00:36:20.000 --> 00:36:21.583
[man yelling in Arabic]

671
00:36:30.708 --> 00:36:31.708
-Hey.

672
00:36:31.792 --> 00:36:32.792
[dramatic score]

673
00:36:34.417 --> 00:36:35.417
Follow that car.

674
00:36:36.167 --> 00:36:36.958
-Copy, sir.

675
00:37:10.875 --> 00:37:11.750
-What's up ahead?

676
00:37:11.833 --> 00:37:12.667
-I don't know.

677
00:37:13.458 --> 00:37:15.708
-[in Chinese]
There's a village there in Area
Four.

678
00:37:15.792 --> 00:37:16.792
But it's dangerous.

679
00:37:18.208 --> 00:37:19.458
-Follow him.

680
00:37:20.583 --> 00:37:22.250
-We're low on fuel.

681
00:37:22.875 --> 00:37:24.292
I can make it, but that's it.

682
00:37:26.167 --> 00:37:28.458
-[in Chinese]
You stay in the helicopter,
okay?

683
00:37:32.667 --> 00:37:33.667
[dune buggy engine revving]

684
00:37:37.250 --> 00:37:38.167
[breathing heavily]

685
00:37:42.167 --> 00:37:43.208
[sighs]

686
00:37:53.333 --> 00:37:54.667
[Arabic conversations
in distance]

687
00:37:54.750 --> 00:37:55.333
[loud grunt]

688
00:37:55.417 --> 00:37:56.417
[glass tinkling on floor]

689
00:38:02.625 --> 00:38:03.875
-Chris, we play.

690
00:38:07.917 --> 00:38:08.750
[tense score]

691
00:38:08.833 --> 00:38:09.667
[goat bleating]

692
00:38:09.750 --> 00:38:11.042
[indistinct conversations]

693
00:38:16.250 --> 00:38:17.875
-[Chris] Almost, bud, almost.

694
00:38:23.708 --> 00:38:24.542
[groans]

695
00:38:26.583 --> 00:38:27.750
Come on, Henry.

696
00:38:30.583 --> 00:38:31.875
That took a bad
hop, took a bad hop.

697
00:38:31.958 --> 00:38:32.875
Oh!

698
00:38:32.958 --> 00:38:34.167
[dramatic score]

699
00:38:51.708 --> 00:38:52.542
You lost?

700
00:38:56.750 --> 00:38:57.917
-I come for my people.

701
00:39:01.583 --> 00:39:03.000
-What are you doing
in my village?

702
00:39:05.000 --> 00:39:06.333
-What are you doing
in the desert?

703
00:39:09.125 --> 00:39:09.958
-I'm fishing.

704
00:39:10.833 --> 00:39:12.167
What are you doing
in the desert?

705
00:39:12.792 --> 00:39:13.792
[cell phone rings]

706
00:39:17.917 --> 00:39:18.917
-[in Chinese] Hello?

707
00:39:19.750 --> 00:39:20.750
I'm fine.

708
00:39:24.000 --> 00:39:26.000
I'm playing baseball
with a <i><font color="white">bangchui </font></i>(idiot).

709
00:39:29.792 --> 00:39:31.125
I came for my people.

710
00:39:32.417 --> 00:39:34.000
-You got the wrong guy.

711
00:39:46.500 --> 00:39:48.125
-Chris, we play.

712
00:39:50.958 --> 00:39:51.792
[goat bleating]

713
00:39:59.250 --> 00:40:00.083
-Whoa.

714
00:40:01.208 --> 00:40:02.208
[tense score
becomes more gentle]

715
00:40:12.167 --> 00:40:13.958
You caught it, Funhouse.
That was awesome.

716
00:40:14.792 --> 00:40:17.458
-[Soraya in Arabic]
I told you many times to behave
yourself.

717
00:40:17.542 --> 00:40:19.125
You will get punished next time.

718
00:40:20.583 --> 00:40:21.833
[in English] Chris,
where are you going?

719
00:40:21.917 --> 00:40:23.750
-I'm going to get our money.
I won't be long.

720
00:40:23.833 --> 00:40:24.667
-Okay.

721
00:40:24.750 --> 00:40:25.583
[engine revving]

722
00:40:26.083 --> 00:40:27.083
[goats bleating]

723
00:40:28.375 --> 00:40:29.375
[dramatic score]

724
00:40:30.708 --> 00:40:31.708
[approaching footsteps]

725
00:40:36.042 --> 00:40:37.042
[retreating footsteps]

726
00:40:37.125 --> 00:40:38.333
[dramatic score]

727
00:40:57.583 --> 00:40:58.292
[gear selector into park]

728
00:41:05.833 --> 00:41:06.875
[door squeaks]

729
00:41:08.542 --> 00:41:09.458
-Yo!

730
00:41:13.625 --> 00:41:14.625
[doors squeak]

731
00:41:15.583 --> 00:41:16.583
[dramatic boom]

732
00:41:25.458 --> 00:41:26.375
[earpiece clicking]

733
00:41:27.833 --> 00:41:28.667
[score fades out]

734
00:41:28.750 --> 00:41:29.750
[blowing wind]

735
00:41:35.542 --> 00:41:36.542
[Chris sighs]

736
00:41:37.708 --> 00:41:38.708
[tender score]

737
00:41:58.792 --> 00:42:00.458
See you on the other side, bro.

738
00:42:00.542 --> 00:42:01.542
[hook and loop fastener ripping]

739
00:42:10.458 --> 00:42:11.458
[feet scuffling]

740
00:42:21.542 --> 00:42:22.542
[tense score]

741
00:42:26.292 --> 00:42:27.542
[pistol rattling]

742
00:43:08.958 --> 00:43:10.083
[grunts and groans]

743
00:43:13.000 --> 00:43:14.000
[exciting score]

744
00:43:24.417 --> 00:43:25.625
Why are you following me?

745
00:43:26.417 --> 00:43:27.708
-Why are you in the desert?

746
00:43:29.375 --> 00:43:29.958
[bones cracking]

747
00:43:35.167 --> 00:43:36.000
[whoosh]

748
00:43:38.333 --> 00:43:39.583
Oh! Ah!

749
00:43:39.667 --> 00:43:40.542
[blade rings]

750
00:43:40.625 --> 00:43:41.792
[grunts]

751
00:43:43.208 --> 00:43:44.000
[grunts and efforts]

752
00:43:46.917 --> 00:43:47.583
[groans]

753
00:43:53.167 --> 00:43:54.125
[whoosh]

754
00:43:57.958 --> 00:43:58.750
Ah.

755
00:43:59.333 --> 00:44:00.625
-[grunts]
-[blade rings]

756
00:44:03.417 --> 00:44:04.292
[blade rings]

757
00:44:09.375 --> 00:44:09.958
Ah!

758
00:44:16.250 --> 00:44:17.292
[whooshing]

759
00:44:26.042 --> 00:44:27.042
You killed my people.

760
00:44:27.125 --> 00:44:29.292
-Ahh, I didn't kill anyone.

761
00:44:29.375 --> 00:44:30.583
-Yes, you did.

762
00:44:31.208 --> 00:44:32.292
-Oh!

763
00:44:40.833 --> 00:44:41.583
Ow!

764
00:44:43.167 --> 00:44:44.208
Uh!

765
00:44:54.250 --> 00:44:55.208
-I know it's you.

766
00:44:55.292 --> 00:44:56.375
-How?

767
00:44:56.667 --> 00:44:57.833
-Fishing in the desert?

768
00:44:58.333 --> 00:44:59.375
Really?

769
00:45:04.042 --> 00:45:04.917
[grunting]

770
00:45:15.417 --> 00:45:16.500
-Listen to me.

771
00:45:19.375 --> 00:45:20.833
Listen to me.

772
00:45:21.458 --> 00:45:22.167
(grunts)

773
00:45:22.250 --> 00:45:23.458
-You killed my people.

774
00:45:23.542 --> 00:45:26.125
-They killed your people.
They killed my brother too.

775
00:45:29.917 --> 00:45:31.500
-[in French] What's
going on here?

776
00:45:31.583 --> 00:45:32.333
Where is my money?

777
00:45:33.875 --> 00:45:34.875
-[in French] Hello.

778
00:45:35.083 --> 00:45:36.083
-You speak French?

779
00:45:36.167 --> 00:45:37.167
-That's all.

780
00:45:37.542 --> 00:45:39.792
-Where is my money, Mr. America?

781
00:45:39.875 --> 00:45:40.708
For the weapons.

782
00:45:40.792 --> 00:45:41.792
-Looking for money?

783
00:45:42.542 --> 00:45:43.792
-Get in line.
-[pin rings]

784
00:45:54.583 --> 00:45:56.375
-Hurry up.
I think they're gonna shoot you.

785
00:45:56.458 --> 00:45:57.292
-Why?

786
00:45:57.375 --> 00:45:58.917
-Because the first
time I see you,

787
00:45:59.000 --> 00:46:00.167
I wanted to shoot you.

788
00:46:06.083 --> 00:46:07.375
-[in French] Start shooting!

789
00:46:09.000 --> 00:46:09.792
-See?

790
00:46:12.250 --> 00:46:13.250
Go!

791
00:46:13.333 --> 00:46:14.333
[dramatic score]

792
00:46:21.167 --> 00:46:22.958
Shit-shit-shit-shit!

793
00:46:23.667 --> 00:46:24.875
-Magazine!
-What?!

794
00:46:24.958 --> 00:46:26.083
-Magazine!

795
00:46:26.750 --> 00:46:27.375
-Here!

796
00:46:28.917 --> 00:46:29.750
